{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-179970-r4516607","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Italian Seasoning","sourcePageId":179970,"sourceRevision":"4516607","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T19:10:50Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Italian%20Seasoning&oldid=4516607","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:05.501Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for spice mixes","Category:Recipes using chile flake","Category:Recipes using marjoram","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"73276b4b988a1b60d96554350ac347e103687e4011eab04f505cdbed05f67f7e","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary\n| category = Spice mix recipes\n| difficulty = 1\n| yield = ¾ cup (180 g)\n}}\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Spices|Spices]]\n\n'''Italian seasoning''' is a dried herb blend traditionally containing basil, oregano, rosemary, thyme, garlic powder, sage, and/or coriander. The blend will differ between recipes and commercial manufacturers.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Basil|Basil]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|Garlic Powder]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Marjoram|Marjoram]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Oregano|Oregano]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Red pepper flakes|Crushed red pepper flakes]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Rosemary|Rosemary]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Sage|Sage]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Savory|Savory]]\n* 1 bunch (20 g) [[Cookbook:Thyme|Thyme]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Mix together well or pulse about a minute in a [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]].\n# Store in an airtight container.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* Start with equal amounts, and modify to your own liking.\n* Basil, marjoram, oregano, and sage are considered essential, but any of the spices are optional.\n* Make only what you need and discard after about a year.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for spice mixes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile flake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marjoram]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Italian Seasoning","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 bunch (20 g) Basil","sourceText":"1 bunch (20 g) Basil","amountText":"1 bunch (20 g) Basil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tablespoons Garlic Powder","sourceText":"2 tablespoons Garlic Powder","amountText":"2 tablespoons Garlic Powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 bunch (20 g) Marjoram","sourceText":"1 bunch (20 g) Marjoram","amountText":"1 bunch (20 g) Marjoram","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 bunch (20 g) Oregano","sourceText":"1 bunch (20 g) Oregano","amountText":"1 bunch (20 g) Oregano","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tablespoons Crushed red pepper flakes","sourceText":"2 tablespoons Crushed red pepper flakes","amountText":"2 tablespoons Crushed red pepper flakes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 bu